  },
  "seamReconciliation": {
    "verdict": "a_mechanical_and_safe",
    "findings": [
      "The pieces are not pieces. Every tile-touching row carries the COMPLETE geometry, byte-identical (equal md5 of geometry::text).",
      "All duplicate rows share county_fips, feature_index, prop_id, owner_name, situs_address, and all four bbox columns.",
      "tile_key parses as 'g0.02:<west_lng>,<south_lat>' -- a regular 0.02-degree grid, fully derivable into a grid position.",
      "Tile membership is exactly predicted by the bbox: 500 of 500 sampled Bastrop tile-spanning features had n_tiles == (floor(east_lng/0.02)-floor(west_lng/0.02)+1)*(floor(north_lat/0.02)-floor(south_lat/0.02)+1), with 0 mismatches.",
      "There is no gap and no overlap to reconcile, because no geometry is ever cut at a tile boundary. Reconciliation is a DISTINCT ON, not a geometric union."
    ],
    "recommendedOperation": "SELECT DISTINCT ON (county_fips, feature_index) ... FROM txgio_parcel ORDER BY county_fips, feature_index, tile_key",
    "namedEdgeCases": [
      "None for the seam operation itself (0 violations statewide).",
      "Separate, non-seam concern: geometry-keyed de-duplication additionally collapses class N5 (many accounts on one identical polygon). If account multiplicity matters downstream, de-duplicate on feature_index for features and keep the account rows alongside."
